> are the files which are in the *ignore* field of the tsconfig still needed to be there now that it's listed as a dependency @eunjae-lee ?

@Haroenv
For example, at `test/mock/createInsightsClient.ts`, it imports files directly from search-insights

```js
import AlgoliaAnalytics from 'search-insights/lib/insights';
import { processQueue } from 'search-insights/lib/_processQueue';
import { getFunctionalInterface } from 'search-insights/lib/_getFunctionalInterface';
```

https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/blob/master/test/mock/createInsightsClient.ts#L1:L4

To clean up `exclude` at tsconfig, we should either

1. export them from search-insights and import them properly in those files
   or
2. search-insights gets the same linting rules and makes no trouble within InstantSearch.js code
